  If there are any Nethack programmer types actively working on
improvements, I have a couple of surface improvments that would be neat...

  One is increasing the message-display to two lines.  I end up hitting ^P a
lot to see what that was that just flashed on and off of the message line as
I jog mindlessly down a corridor.  With two lines, something could pop on
screen, then you move, and it gets pushed up one line until a new message
comes (just leaving old messages on screen until a new message comes would
work, but then you couldn't tell if you had 1 message that had been there
for 2 minutes, or maybe the same message just keeps on coming every 10
seconds...)
  Secondly, I think it would be cool to describe combat a little more. 
Specifically:
  Do whatever sort of things you do to see if the player gets hit by a
monster.  Calculate this based on some average Dexterity rating and no
armor.
  Do it again, this time taking any dexterity bonuses/penalites into
account.  If they would have gotten hit before, but won't now, due to
dexterity, we could see "The goblin swings, but you duck and he misses!" or
"The goblin swings, but you deftly step aside!"
  Calculate again, this time taking armor class into account.  If the player
would have gotten hit before, but now won't take damage because of their AC,
we could see things like "The goblin swings, but you block the blow with
your shield!" or "The goblin swings, but it just bounces off of your
helmet!" or "The goblin swings, but your scale mail deflects the hit!" 
Exactly which piece of armor does the actual stoppage could be figured
randomly...
 
  Also... does AC just decrease the chance of being hit, or does it also
decrease actual damage done when hit?  IMHO, I think heavier armors would
actually *increase* hit probability for the attacker, but when you're
sitting in a tank, all the pointy objects in the world won't do much.
(how can someone miss you when you're standing there in a enormous suit of
plate mail that weighs five times more than you can bench press?:)

  Oh, heck, while I'm here...
  This is an idea stolen from Moria:  make some items effectively weigh less
when worn.  Boots for instance, unless made of cement, aren't going to
matter much with regards to encumberance while worn.  Plate mail would weigh
significantly less when worn than when carried in a backpack, since it
practically supports itself.  Chain mail, though, since it just hangs off of
you, would weigh the same.  You'd have to go along and try to guess just how
much various types of armor support their own weight when worn, but well,
that's where all the fun is anyway.  =)



